412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: todowrite]\n[tool: bash]\nDelegating the inventory/members investigation to a subagent while I look at the others.\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: task]\n[tool: todowrite]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: todowrite]\n`python3 -m unittest` now passes all 16 tests. It was 15 before because `test_search.py` couldn't be imported and counted as one error; it actually holds two tests. I only changed code in `catalog/` and left the tests alone.\n\nFixes:\n- **`catalog/search.py:3`**: the file imported `normalize` from a module that doesn't exist, `catalog.nonexistent`. It now imports it from `catalog.text`.\n- **`catalog/books.py:22`**: `parse_book` stored the year as text. It now converts it to a whole number with `int(year)`.\n- **`catalog/factory.py`**: added the missing third sample book, `Emma` by Austen. I picked 1815 and 1 copy; the tests only check the title.\n- **`catalog/fees.py:14`**: the fee added the daily rate to the days late instead of multiplying, so it now uses `days_late * DAILY_FEE`.\n- **`catalog/inventory.py:24`**: `recent(n)` returned one event too many. It now returns the last `n`. I also made `recent(0)` return an empty list, because the fixed slice would otherwise return the whole history. No test covers that case.\n- **`catalog/members.py:4`**: `MAX_BORROWED` was 3, but the comment above it and the tests both say members can hold five books. It's now 5.\n\nAs you asked, a subagent investigated the `test_inventory` and `test_members` failures and found the causes of the last two fixes; I made the changes myself.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_